#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Omarchy Window Geometry Persistence, Dynamic Screen Adaptation & Click-Raise Daemon:
1. All main application windows open in MAXIMIZED view by default (unless previously tiled or resized).
2. Dialogue boxes, popups, and utility windows open floating and centered without being maximized.
3. If a window was tiled 50% (left/right/top/bottom) or quarter-tiled, it restores to that exact 50% / quarter
   layout on whatever monitor it is opened on, adjusting width and height to match the new screen dimensions.
4. If a window was custom resized, it scales proportionally to the new monitor resolution while staying fully in bounds.
5. Remembers states dynamically across restarts and monitor changes.
6. Pure floating management (fullscreen = 0) in Hyprland's unified Floating Layer for Windows 11 Z-stack raising.
"""

